sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P as Priya
    actor R as Desk Lead or Senior Handler
    participant A as Ada (chat model)
    participant S as Memory store
    participant W as Scheduler
    participant C as Refine cycle
    participant B as Background model

    rect rgb(10, 32, 52)
    Note over P,S: The day — retain. Nothing is learned on the turn.
    P->>A: a request (an Amber Pack, an upload, a customer update, a remark)
    A->>S: read what is known
    A-->>P: reply
    A->>S: write the episode: messages, tool calls, the run
    end

    rect rgb(34, 16, 52)
    Note over S,B: The night — refine. No user is waiting.
    W->>C: cycle is due (skipped if nobody has spoken since the last one)
    loop eleven jobs, in a fixed order
        C->>S: read transcripts and existing memory
        C->>B: propose changes for this job
        B-->>C: proposals
        C->>C: code checks them (quotes, source levels, gates)
        C->>S: apply what its rule allows, flag or queue the rest
    end
    C->>S: store one report: changed, flagged, waiting, tokens
    end

    rect rgb(10, 40, 24)
    Note over P,S: The morning — review, recall and reuse.
    R->>C: approve what is waiting, read what was flagged
    C->>S: apply what they approve, under their name
    P->>A: the next request
    A->>S: read the tidied memory
    A-->>P: a better-informed reply
    end
